# ─── Rust ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/target
**/target

# Cargo.lock is deliberately NOT ignored: this workspace builds binaries (the CLI), so reproducible
# dependency resolution matters. The intent is stated here because the file is absent -- generating it
# needs network to a registry the environment that produced this branch could not reach -- and an
# earlier version of this comment claimed it was already committed, which was false. If it is ever
# added to the ignore list, that is a decision to make loudly, not a line to slip in.

# ─── Python (research + pack tooling) ───────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ─── Node / TypeScript (@chiti/voice-web, Voice Lab — Phase 3+) ─────
node_modules/
*.tsbuildinfo
apps/voice-lab/dist/
packages/voice-web/dist/

# ─── Editors / OS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# ─── Local scratch output ───────────────────────────────────────────
/out
/bench-results
# voice-packs/dist/*.cvpack are tracked deliverables — do NOT ignore dist/ wholesale.

# ─── Model weights ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Real ONNX models are large binary assets (tens to hundreds of MB) and do not
# belong in git. They are delivered via releases/LFS/a pack registry, then
# assembled into .cvpack by scripts/build-voice-packs.py.
voice-packs/**/*.onnx
voice-packs/**/*.onnx.data

# ─── Signing material (Phase 11) ────────────────────────────────────
*.key
*.pem
/signing/

# Model assets fetched by scripts/fetch-offline-model.py (88 MB+ weights never belong in git;
# the .cvpack format exists so model bytes travel beside a manifest, not in history)
models/
